THIRD-PARTY NOTICES — IMPORTANT FOR shogi_engine

The `engine/bin/shogi_engine` binary links the vendored cshogi C++ core
(`engine/third_party/cshogi-upstream/`, `engine/third_party/cshogi_core/`),
which is derived from Apery (itself derived from Stockfish) and licensed
under **GNU GPL v3**. Binary distributions of shogi_engine therefore inherit
GPL v3 obligations. See cshogi-upstream/LICENSE for full terms.

The chess_engine binary, training pipeline, GUI, and non-shogi headers
link only against:
  - Disservin/chess-library (MIT)
  - ml-explore/mlx + ml-explore/mlx-c (MIT)
  - nlohmann/json (MIT)
  - python-chess, pygame, mlx (all permissive)
and are therefore MIT-only.

If you plan to redistribute shogi_engine, ensure compliance with GPL v3.
If you need a non-GPL shogi engine, substitute a non-GPL move generator
(e.g. write from scratch or use a permissively-licensed alternative).
